# AGENT INSTRUCTION SET: DeepSeek 4.1 Flash + ECC + Superpowers + UI UX Pro Max

## 1. CORE OPERATIONAL WORKFLOW (Superpowers Protocol)
- **Phase 1: Brainstorm & Spec First.** Do NOT write code immediately for complex features. Ask clarifying questions and propose a technical spec first.
- **Phase 2: Planning.** Break implementations down into small, distinct, 2-to-5 minute execution steps with clear pass/fail conditions.
- **Phase 3: Test-Driven Development (TDD).** Write failing test cases prior to implementing production logic.
- **Phase 4: Systematic Debugging.** Formulate hypotheses, inspect logs/traces, and identify root causes before attempting code changes.

## 2. DESIGN & STYLING RULES (UI UX Pro Max Protocol)
- Follow design guidelines and color palette rules located in `.agents/` and `.cline/skills/`.
- Enforce strict visual hierarchy, responsive Tailwind/CSS rules, and accessibility standards.

## 3. CODE QUALITY & PATTERNS (Everything Claude Code Protocol)
- Maintain code modularity, strict type definitions, and follow language-specific security guardrails located in `.cline/skills/`.

## 4. SKILL DIRECTORY REFERENCE
All sub-skills and detailed domain rules are stored in `.cline/skills/`. Refer to specific markdown files in this directory when invoked.

## Skill-use policy

- Before starting a task, inspect available project skills and identify only
  the skills relevant to the task.
- State which skills will be loaded and why before writing files or running
  commands.
- Do not claim compliance with a skill unless its SKILL.md or required
  referenced instruction has been loaded and followed.
- Do not load UI/UX, accessibility, cloud AI, deployment, or other unrelated
  skills for backend-only tasks.
- Always load `verification-before-completion` before declaring any milestone,
  feature, build, test suite, migration, backup, restore, or release complete.
- Load `systematic-debugging` after a failed test, build, runtime command, or
  unexpected behavior and before proposing a code change.
- For authentication, roles, sessions, secrets, cloud AI, file uploads, or
  permissions, load the relevant security skill before implementation or review.
- For schema/database changes, load the database migration/integrity skill.
- For user-facing forms, POS, scanner workflows, reports, dashboards, and
  Android browser screens, load UI/UX and accessibility skills.